\fs34\b RiqatonyDesk\b0\fs22\par\par
\par
RiqatonyDesk 1.0.0-x11.2 is a Ribbon-based RTF editor with workspace navigation,\par
Open documents now survive external delete or rename-away through a shared live-path safety monitor; missing backing files remain protected until preserved, explicitly recreated, or explicitly closed.\par
folder dashboards, background discovery, and conservative file handling. It\par
stores ordinary .rtf files and does not introduce a private document format.\par
\par
\fs27\b Highlights\b0\fs22\par
\par
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Registered workspaces with a recursive sidebar and fast switching\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Dynamic Workspace(s) quick selector; inactive roots are never scanned\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Workspace and folder dashboards in List or Grid view\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Exactly two card actions: Open and View Only\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab One rich-text Ribbon with File, Home, Insert, View, and Help tabs\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Full-width Ribbon above the sidebar and document/dashboard surface\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Riqa Icons Heritage, Humility, and Harmony, each with light and dark variants; all three are available from Settings \u8594? App Icons and Configure, and Modern remains the default\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Searchable shortcuts with case-insensitive, modifier-order-independent matching\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Safe create, duplicate, rename, move, import, and removal operations\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Dirty Duplicate and External Editor choices distinguish the current unsaved document from the last saved disk version, with remembered policies under Settings\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab F2 renames either the active RTF file or the selected Workspace subfolder\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Atomic RTF saving, external-change detection, and bounded file loading\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Save, Save As, Save and New, Save and Dashboard, and Save and Exit\par\li0\fi0
\li360\fi-180\bullet\tab Standards-based RTF lists plus curated LibreOffice interoperability coverage\par\li0\fi0
\par
\fs27\b Run from source\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par
\f1\fs19 python3 -m venv .venv\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 source .venv/bin/activate\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 python -m pip install -r riqatony_desk/requirements.txt\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 python main.py\par\f0\fs22
\par
\par
Useful launch forms:\par
\par
\par
\f1\fs19 python main.py --version\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 python main.py --setup\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 python main.py document.rtf\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 python main.py --open-file document.rtf\par\f0\fs22
\par
\par
Starting without a file opens the Dashboard and creates no document. New RTF\par
File asks the editor layer to create a complete, valid RTF document; RiqatonyDesk\par
never uses an empty placeholder file.\par
\par
\fs27\b Workspaces and OS file opening\b0\fs22\par
\par
Only the active workspace is scanned. An RTF opened by the operating system\par
inside that workspace uses its normal workspace entry. An RTF outside the\par
workspace opens as a transient external session: it is not copied, imported,\par
or added to workspace navigation or dashboards.\par
\par
External RTF drops use explicit destinations. Drop onto the Dashboard button, Main Dashboard, or empty sidebar tree to import to the Workspace root; drop onto a sidebar folder to import to that folder; drop onto a sidebar file to import to that file's containing folder; and drop onto a Folder Dashboard to import to that folder. Dropping a supported RTF onto the editor opens it through RiqatonyDesk' external-file lifecycle instead of importing it. Unrelated application chrome rejects drops. Internal managed-document drag-to-move uses the same sidebar destination rules: folder row to that folder, file row to that file's containing folder, and empty tree or Dashboard button to Workspace root.\par
\par
Ctrl+O opens workspace management. RiqatonyDesk has no separate Open RTF\par
Document command; desktop file associations and workspace navigation cover\par
that workflow.\par
\par
\fs27\b AppImage\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par
\f1\fs19 ./riqatony_desk/packaging/fedora/install-build-deps.sh\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 ./riqatony_desk/packaging/fedora/build-appimage.sh\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 chmod +x riqatony_desk/dist/RiqatonyDesk-1.0.0-x11.2-x86_64.AppImage\par\f0\fs22
\f1\fs19 ./riqatony_desk/dist/RiqatonyDesk-1.0.0-x11.2-x86_64.AppImage\par\f0\fs22
\par
\par
The desktop launcher accepts one RTF path through %f. Files outside the active workspace open as transient external sessions; AppImage mode keeps configuration and documents outside the read-only bundle.\par
\par
\fs27\b Configuration and diagnostics\b0\fs22\par
\par
Configuration uses the independent per-user RiqatonyDesk directory\par
~/.config/brunonlinespace/riqatonydesk, without reading old Rico Plus\par
preferences. Optional shutdown timing is enabled with:\par
\par
\par
\f1\fs19 RIQATONYDESK_PROFILE_SHUTDOWN=1 python main.py\par\f0\fs22
\par
\par
\fs27\b Validation\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par
\f1\fs19 python -m riqatony_desk.tools.release_check\par\f0\fs22
\par
\par
See QA.md, BUILDING.md, and RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md for the complete gates.\par
\par
\fs27\b Documentation command\b0\fs22\par
\par
Help \u8594? Documentation opens the bundled Documentation.rtf as a transient external RiqatonyDesk document in its own window. The source-tree Markdown files in docs/ remain developer/release documentation and are not the user-facing Help document.\par
